1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:06,767
Long conversations leave us with conclusions, but their supporting context is easy to lose.

2
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:11,836
Bridge keeps memory, source material, and actual model activity together.

3
00:00:11,836 --> 00:00:16,700
Here is the Otari edition, using results from real hosted validation.

4
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:23,928
The project reuses its existing Markdown knowledge base and SQLite state.

5
00:00:23,928 --> 00:00:30,442
Otari provides hosted inference, with separate roles for extraction, synthesis, and tools.

6
00:00:30,442 --> 00:00:36,045
Each research task saves its question, source versions, and prepared requests.

7
00:00:36,045 --> 00:00:43,194
After an interruption, the task can continue from saved steps, keeping the evidence it already collected.

8
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:53,234
This recorded evidence view shows a saved question: does the remote demonstration policy contain real customer records?

9
00:00:53,234 --> 00:00:57,749
The answer is no, supported by the document's explicit statement.

10
00:00:57,749 --> 00:01:05,707
Opening the citation reveals the versioned source. The English passage shown here translates the original Chinese evidence.

11
00:01:05,707 --> 00:01:11,700
The ledger preserves the actual model, request identifiers, and provider-reported charges.

12
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:21,180
An exact quotation proves that a passage exists. It does not automatically prove that every conclusion is correct.

13
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:30,024
A candidate passes structure, quotation, and semantic checks. One revision is allowed; a second rejection prevents publication.

14
00:01:30,024 --> 00:01:34,441
A stable business key alone cannot guarantee exactly-once refunds.

15
00:01:34,441 --> 00:01:41,700
Unrelated questions receive insufficient evidence. Remote-only mode also excludes identical local text.

16
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:49,853
A hosted search retrieved Python's official documentation and saved an inspectable page revision.

17
00:01:49,853 --> 00:01:56,736
Code analysis consumed the actual call ledger and returned sandbox output with a successful exit status.

18
00:01:56,736 --> 00:02:01,774
Execution is marked verified only when an observable tool result is available.

19
00:02:01,774 --> 00:02:09,922
Each step retains its request identifier. Fluent model prose never substitutes for a missing execution record.

20
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:21,423
An isolated routing policy sent a deliberately incompatible model request to test cross-provider fallback.

21
00:02:21,423 --> 00:02:27,636
DeepInfra returned a real four-oh-four. Otari recorded that failed attempt as absorbed.

22
00:02:27,636 --> 00:02:35,834
Nebius then succeeded on attempt two. The application received the fallback flag, attempt count, and actual charge.

23
00:02:35,834 --> 00:02:43,062
This was a controlled pre-answer failure, not a provider outage or a guarantee that every streaming failure can recover.

24
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:54,372
The complete validation cost was about twelve cents, including failed exploration, reviews, and revisions.

25
00:02:54,372 --> 00:03:01,880
The workspace retains its twenty-cent cumulative ceiling, across every provider, without resetting spent funds.

26
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:10,700
The pre-synthesis snapshot excludes the current synthesis, review, and later analysis. Whole-task cost comes from the call ledger.

27
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:18,677
The remote MCP demonstration exposed one fictional refund policy through three read-only tools.

28
00:03:18,677 --> 00:03:25,170
Completed searches, source reads, and versions were saved, allowing a new question to reuse that evidence.

29
00:03:25,170 --> 00:03:31,426
Without an eligible remote source, the application returns insufficient evidence and makes no model call.

30
00:03:31,426 --> 00:03:39,700
The temporary endpoint is now closed. These are retained validation results; the personal knowledge base has not been republished.

31
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:47,229
Check the memory. Resume the research. Explain the cost.

32
00:03:47,229 --> 00:03:53,882
The code, observed failures, and hosted acceptance evidence are available on the public competition branch.

33
00:03:53,882 --> 00:03:58,140
Bridge connects useful personal memory to a record you can inspect.
